cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'AIDE-SAI-link: a CESM-forced TOMAS-JAX sectional aerosol model with interactive aerosol-radiation-microphysics coupling for stratospheric aerosol injection'
abstract: >-
  A GPU (JAX) sectional stratospheric aerosol model forced by prescribed CESM
  meteorology. Carries 40 TOMAS size bins in two moments plus SO2 and H2SO4,
  with continuous SO2 injection, SO2-OH chemistry, nucleation, condensation,
  Brownian coagulation, gravitational settling through an open band bottom,
  Lin-Rood flux-form transport, and RRTMGP radiative transfer with Mie optics
  on the wet H2SO4/H2O droplet. Aerosol, radiation and microphysics are
  interactively coupled: radiative heating from the model's own aerosol
  accumulates into the temperature seen by the microphysics, by settling, and
  by the next radiation call. The forcing is one-way only with respect to the
  meteorology - the winds are prescribed, so the circulation does not respond.
